# MCUHome Matter framework component (docs/design/component-model.md §2,
# "core" kind): wires upstream CHIP (connectedhomeip) into the MCUHome
# runtime — PSA crypto, Thread/OpenThread defaults, dynamic-endpoint
# support, and the runtime that turns the builder's generated tables
# (ADR 0014, <mcuhome/matter_tables.h>) into registered Matter endpoints.

menuconfig MCUHOME_MATTER
	bool "MCUHome Matter framework"
	depends on CHIP
	depends on MCUHOME
	# CHIP's own Kconfig (modules/lib/connectedhomeip/config/zephyr/Kconfig)
	# does `imply NEWLIB_LIBC_NANO` — an *imply*, not a hard `select`, and
	# LIBC_IMPLEMENTATION is a `choice`: choice symbols can never be
	# `select`ed, by upstream or by us, only steered via `default`/prompt.
	# On nRF52840 the newlib-nano default heap setup dies pre-main
	# (bisected 2026-08-03), before any of our code — or even the rest of
	# Kconfig — gets a chance to react. There is no runtime hook left to
	# catch this once it happens. Depending on PICOLIBC here instead turns
	# a silent pre-main crash on the bench into a loud configure-time
	# dependency error (missing CONFIG_PICOLIBC=y) at `west build` time.
	depends on PICOLIBC
	# CHIP's UDP endpoints need IPv6 packet info (recvmsg ancillary data) to
	# answer from the correct source address; without this option the
	# IPV6_RECVPKTINFO setsockopt fails (errno 109) and PASE handshakes die
	# silently — the commissioner sees "address unreachable".
	select NET_CONTEXT_RECV_PKTINFO
	# SLAAC is off in vanilla Zephyr (NCS turns it on): without it the device
	# never gets an address from the border router's OMR prefix, and the SRP
	# server rejects the host registration ("internal server error") — the
	# node is then invisible to Matter on-network discovery.
	select OPENTHREAD_SLAAC if NET_L2_OPENTHREAD
	help
	  Enables the MCUHome Matter (CHIP) integration: PSA crypto wiring,
	  Thread/OpenThread defaults and the dynamic-endpoint runtime that the
	  builder drives from generated device tables. See
	  docs/design/matter-zephyr-integration.md for the findings behind
	  the defaults this symbol pulls in.

if MCUHOME_MATTER

config MCUHOME_MATTER_PSA_WANTS
	bool
	default y if MBEDTLS
	# The PSA_WANT_* symbols are promptless while MBEDTLS_PROMPTLESS is
	# active — plain prj.conf assignments are silently dropped. An app
	# Kconfig `select` is the supported way to force them on. CHIP needs
	# HKDF (SPAKE2+ key derivation — missing it kills PASE with a silent
	# INTERNAL after the point math), ECDH (CASE), SHA-1 (certificates)
	# and PBKDF2 (PASE prover side).
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_HKDF
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_ECDH
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_SHA_1
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_PBKDF2_HMAC
	select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_DERIVE
	select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_HMAC

choice MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_ROLE
	prompt "Thread device role"
	depends on NET_L2_OPENTHREAD
	default MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_ROUTER
	help
	  CHIP ThreadStackManager device role, set at startup via
	  ConnectivityManager::SetThreadDeviceType(). Sleepy End Device (SED)
	  support is not offered here yet — it lands with the power-management
	  phase (ICD configuration, poll period, Matter LIT/SIT semantics).

config MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_ROUTER
	bool "Router (FTD)"
	help
	  Full Thread Device: participates in mesh routing, radio always on.
	  Correct choice for mains-powered nodes.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_MED
	bool "Minimal End Device (MED)"
	help
	  Minimal End Device: does not route for other devices, but (unlike a
	  Sleepy End Device) keeps its radio on. Use this for battery-powered
	  nodes until SED support lands.

endchoice

config MCUHOME_MATTER_TEST_DAC
	bool "Use CHIP's example device attestation credentials"
	default y
	help
	  Registers connectedhomeip's example Device Attestation Credentials
	  provider (test PAA/PAI/DAC from the Matter test certificate space).
	  This is ADR 0012 path A: development and pre-alpha use test
	  certificates; MCUHome's own attestation root — with per-device DACs
	  provisioned into a protected partition — is a v1.0 deliverable.

	  Nodes built with this option commission only against controllers
	  that accept test certificates (Home Assistant, chip-tool and
	  matter.js do; certified ecosystems do not).

	  Disabling this symbol without linking an alternative provider is a
	  build error: a node with no attestation provider fails
	  commissioning at the attestation step with no useful diagnostic.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_INIT_RETRY_FOREVER
	bool "Retry failing bring-up stages forever"
	default y
	help
	  Development behavior, kept from the E2E prototype: when a CHIP
	  bring-up stage fails, log it and retry indefinitely instead of
	  giving up. This gives an attached debugger unlimited reproduction
	  windows without a reset dance, and it keeps a node that boots
	  before its network is ready from bricking itself into a reboot
	  loop.

	  With this disabled, mcuhome_matter_start() returns on the first
	  failing stage and the application decides what to do. Table
	  validation errors are never retried either way.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MAX_DYNAMIC_ENDPOINTS
	int "Maximum number of dynamically registered endpoints"
	default 4
	range 1 32
	help
	  Sizes the framework's endpoint translation pools AND CHIP's own
	  dynamic endpoint registry
	  (CHIP_DEVICE_CONFIG_DYNAMIC_ENDPOINT_COUNT, see
	  include/mcuhome/matter/chip_project_config.h) — deliberately the
	  same symbol for both: if CHIP's registry is the smaller one,
	  registration still reports success but the endpoint's Descriptor
	  cluster instance is dropped upstream without an error (ADR 0014).

	  Endpoint 0 (the root node) is static and not counted here.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MAX_CLUSTERS_PER_ENDPOINT
	int "Maximum number of server clusters per endpoint"
	default 4
	range 2 32
	help
	  INCLUDING the Descriptor cluster the framework appends to every
	  endpoint, so the usable budget for generated table clusters is one
	  less than this value.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MAX_ATTRS_PER_ENDPOINT
	int "Maximum number of attribute metadata slots per endpoint"
	default 16
	range 4 256
	help
	  Sizes the per-endpoint EmberAfAttributeMetadata pool. Every table
	  cluster costs its own attributes PLUS two global ones (FeatureMap
	  and ClusterRevision, which the framework serves from the cluster's
	  feature_map/cluster_revision fields), and the appended Descriptor
	  cluster costs one more.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MAX_DEVICE_TYPES_PER_ENDPOINT
	int "Maximum number of device types per endpoint"
	default 2
	range 1 8
	help
	  Sizes the per-endpoint EmberAfDeviceType pool. One entry is enough
	  for a plain device type; a second covers a device type plus a
	  namespace/derived type.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MAX_PENDING_REPORTS
	int "Maximum number of in-flight attribute change reports"
	default 8
	range 1 64
	help
	  mcuhome_matter_attr_changed() hands the reporting call to the CHIP
	  event loop instead of calling into the stack from the application
	  thread, and needs one slot per change that has been queued but not
	  yet processed. When all slots are taken the change report is
	  dropped with a warning — the attribute value itself is unaffected
	  and the next report re-synchronises the controller.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_DNSSD_RETRY_INTERVAL_S
	int "DNS-SD advertisement retry interval (seconds)"
	default 30
	range 1 3600
	help
	  See CONFIG_MCUHOME_MATTER_DNSSD_RETRY_COUNT.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_DNSSD_RETRY_COUNT
	int "Number of DNS-SD advertisement retries after startup"
	default 10
	range 0 100
	help
	  Workaround for an upstream gap (candidate C7): on the OpenThread
	  platform nothing ever posts kDnssdInitialized/kDnssdRestartNeeded,
	  so a commissionable-node advertisement that fails during
	  Server::Init() is never retried and the node stays undiscoverable
	  forever. Observed live on 2026-08-05: the first advertisement fails
	  because the SRP client has not started yet, and the node recovers
	  on a later retry once SRP is up.

	  The framework therefore re-runs the DNS-SD server start this many
	  times, CONFIG_MCUHOME_MATTER_DNSSD_RETRY_INTERVAL_S apart
	  (defaults cover the first five minutes after boot).
	  Re-registration is idempotent. Set to 0 to disable once the
	  upstream event is fixed.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MRP_ACTIVE_RETRY_MS
	int "Advertised MRP active retry interval (ms)"
	default 4000
	range 100 60000
	help
	  CHIP_CONFIG_MRP_LOCAL_ACTIVE_RETRY_INTERVAL. Software SPAKE2+ needs
	  ~3.2 s per step on a plain Cortex-M33; with the Thread default
	  (SAI 2 s) the commissioner's retransmission budget expires first
	  and commissioning fails as "address unreachable". Raise, don't
	  lower, unless the node has hardware crypto acceleration.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_MRP_IDLE_RETRY_MS
	int "Advertised MRP idle retry interval (ms)"
	default 5000
	range 100 60000
	help
	  CHIP_CONFIG_MRP_LOCAL_IDLE_RETRY_INTERVAL. Same rationale as
	  CONFIG_MCUHOME_MATTER_MRP_ACTIVE_RETRY_MS.

endif # MCUHOME_MATTER
